WEBVTT

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:42.720
Oh, Fujicakes! Mwah!

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.560
Wh-Wh-What the... What?

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.310
Hey, Lupin.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.740
The can's busted.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.990
<b>Fujiko's Gift</b>

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:24.320
You broke the toi-let! You broke the toi-let!

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.710
It was already busted when I went in there.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:29.990
What has happened?

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:32.590
Hey, Goemon. You're awake?

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:33.900
I just woke up.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:37.630
Something's stuck in the 
toilet's drainage pipe, it seems.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:41.590
I tried poking around with some chopsticks, 
but no luck. We're outta options.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:42.810
Chopsticks?

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.210
Yeah. One of your disposable pairs.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.120
That was my last pair!

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.980
Use a freakin' fork, then!

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.730
The repairman said he'd be here soon, right?

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:57.920
Wouldn't count on it. They say French 
handymen like to take their sweet time.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.160
So what do we do?

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.650
Well...

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.850
I'm gonna use yours instead!

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.350
It's my room! That means I get to go first!

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:12.810
You just went, didn't you?!

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.610
I still need to go!

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.220
Hold it!

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:19.390
No leaving the room without 
a disguise. You know that.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:22.250
That's the rule. When we leave the hideout,

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:25.270
we make sure we're disguised as a pair 
of charming middle-aged silver foxes.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.950
I'm just going to my room downstairs, man.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:32.160
It's <i>precisely</i> in those moments that 
you walk face-first into trouble, you know?

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.400
Boy, I'm really gonna miss this place...

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:39.640
You'll cover the moving costs, of course.

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.260
Damn it all!

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.190
I'm going first.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.310
Son of a...

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.850
What do you think?

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:57.760
Can you even see where you are going?

00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:59.100
Perfect.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:05.200
Huh?

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.600
Hey, it's only me. Open this door, will ya?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.650
Hey! Open up, Go, my boy!

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:13.980
What's wrong?

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.180
This jerk locked the door!

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.920
I tried to get in and he just 
said, "identify yourself."

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.680
Caution is a virtue.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.060
You're still mad about 
the chopsticks, aren't ya?

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.560
What a child.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:27.960
What?!

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:31.450
Just buy him some more, Lupin.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:35.730
Anyway, what're we gonna 
do for food? Wanna eat out?

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:39.870
Well, we don't know when 
the handyman's gonna show up.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.470
Should we cook?

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:42.670
Japanese food.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:44.980
Gonna eat with your hands?

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.340
Don't start, you two.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.050
What about takeout sushi?

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:54.320
I don't think there's a place 
near here that delivers.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.920
Why would you choose such 
an unsuitable place as our hideout?

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:59.020
'Cause sushi isn't a priority.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:05.440
Come to think of it, I think the first-floor 
café has Japanese cuisine on the menu.

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.980
The one run by that married couple?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:12.200
I heard the owner say he needed buckwheat 
flour. The kind you use for soba noodles.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:15.850
Oh? You going down there, Goemon?

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:17.770
There is no need for you to accompany me.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:19.630
Hey, what about a disguise?

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:22.510
I came in without one. 
It should not pose any problems.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:26.400
Hey, if you get spotted on the way out, 
it means you can't come back in.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:32.140
At least throw this on.

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:37.920
Now you're our granddaughter!

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:40.660
Idiocy.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.680
You sure they have Japanese food?

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:46.030
Oh, yeah! You bet!

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:50.830
There wasn't any...

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:54.370
C'mon, they <i>must've</i> had 
something. Did you even ask?

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.200
I did.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:58.530
I asked for the dish that 
contained buckwheat flour.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:00.130
And they gave it to you, right?

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.680
So? What was it?

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:10.460
You gotta make a song and dance
out of everything, don'tcha?

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:16.380
It looked like this.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:18.320
Oh, the galettes!

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:20.190
Those are pretty good.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:20.990
Indeed, it was.

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:23.080
So you liked it?

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:25.220
But it wasn't Japanese food.

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.730
But it <i>was</i> good, yes?

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.980
It was indeed good, but you deceived me.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:37.120
I'm going back to my room.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:39.750
What?!

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.280
Let me use your bathroom first.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.700
What the hell is with you always needing 
to go when I do?! Mix it up a little!

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.360
We eat the same food at the same time! 
What do you want from me?!

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:49.530
You, too?!

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:50.720
I require the facilities.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.130
Okay, rock, paper, scissors it is!

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:58.150
Mornin'...

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:01.860
What?

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:02.780
Fujiko!

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.760
What is it?! Buzz off!

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.270
The toilet's busted!

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:17.170
Where's the bucket?

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:23.810
Would it kill you to put up 
an "out of order" sign?

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.390
When'd you get here, Fujiko?

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.200
You let me in yesterday, Lupin.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.530
I did?

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:37.470
You were drunk as a skunk, though.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:41.700
This new hideout's pretty nice.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:42.680
Ain't it?

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:45.930
You wanna move in?

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:48.690
She moves in, I move out.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.540
The floorboards are pretty chunky. 
You won't hear a thing.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:55.570
That's not what I'm worried about.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.870
Why the hell is <i>she</i> here?!

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.460
I dunno! To celebrate us moving in?

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.850
And she sneaks in unnoticed to do this?

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.910
She says I let her in...

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:10.790
And did you?!

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.880
I don't remember.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:13.670
What?!

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:14.710
I give up! I give up, I give up!

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:15.730
Suspicious.

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:17.790
What's suspicious?

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:20.180
Put some clothes on.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.400
I'm wearing some.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.080
Wow, nice view!

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:23.720
Hey!

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:26.660
What are you scheming?

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.860
<b>Incoming
 Call</b>

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.860
<b>Plumber</b>

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:33.950
Gimme a sec...

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:38.160
Ahoy-hoy. You the handyman?

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.860
What? You can't make it for a while?

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:42.820
Well, that's no good. Yeah.

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:46.170
Yeah, something in the drainage pipe. Right.

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:50.050
The one between the tank and the commode...

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:50.420
<b>Plumber</b>

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:53.050
What's the big idea, Fujiko?

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:56.520
Letting a total stranger 
into your hideout?

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:59.050
You're getting careless, Lupin.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:01.160
Says a total stranger in our hideout.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.060
Wow...

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:04.810
But it's kinda inconvenient 
not being able to use the can, y'know?

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.330
I'll just use the one in Jigen's room.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:08.880
Not happening.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.460
Well, I need a shower.

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:12.680
The toilet's out of action,
 but there's still hot water, right?

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:22.660
Fujiko's hiding something, isn't she?

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:23.600
Yeah...

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:26.700
When I peeked in on her,
 I heard her on the phone.

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:31.830
Mr. Handyman, the toilet's working now, 
so you don't have to come over.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:34.270
But Grampy said to say thank you!

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:35.440
What age was she going for?

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:37.210
So she's the granddaughter now?

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.060
She doesn't want anyone in that bathroom.

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:42.770
The stuff about taking 
a shower was just a cover.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:45.170
What could she be hiding?

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:46.370
Who knows?

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:49.310
But it's gotta be some kind of object.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:51.730
In the toilet's cistern.

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:56.470
She snuck in yesterday without us noticing 
and squirreled something away in there.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:58.860
And now, it's stuck in the pipe.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:00.300
Something dangerous?

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:01.270
Could be loot.

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:03.230
I am in the "something dangerous" camp.

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:07.740
Either way, I don't like the fact
she's trying to hide it from us.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.970
Hey, maybe she wanted it to be a surprise.

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:12.740
A surprise? One that goes "boom," you mean?

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:14.550
Explosives?!

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:17.750
Well... with Fujiko, you can't rule it out.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:21.160
Go ask her what's up, Jigen.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.540
Why me?

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:24.000
Chalk it up as life experience.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.790
Fujiko's your territory. None of my business.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:33.510
Fine, fine. I get it.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.410
I need to use the can.

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.780
You're gonna talk to Fujiko first.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:41.650
Gonna burst! Gonna burst! 
It'll go everywhere!

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:43.960
Very well, then.

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:46.680
Try and be subtle, yeah?

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:52.860
Fujiko. What have you hidden in our toilet?

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:54.630
I said "subtle"!

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:56.660
Goemon?!

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:08.430
I'm not hiding anything.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.430
Wow!

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:12.580
Wouldn't kill you to hide <i>certain</i> things...

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:30.260
Well, now...

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:32.990
Guess I should go shower, too.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.760
Just a minute, Lupin...

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.580
You can't wait any longer, either?

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:41.260
Bingo...

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:43.960
Wanna play Strip Old Maid?

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:45.670
You bet!

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:47.260
Wrapped around her little finger.

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:49.590
There we go!

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:52.530
I win!

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:54.540
Dammit!

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.690
Come on, take 'em off.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.520
Huh? Where are you going?

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:04.270
I need to dry my hair. No peeking now!

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.330
She's holed up in the bathroom again.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:11.800
I guess that means she hasn't 
been able to recover the stuff.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:17.860
Something smells great!

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:19.760
What the heck are you doing, man?

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.520
I got the café owner to 
give me some buckwheat.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:23.810
For noodles?

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.930
I will empty... my mind...

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:31.020
You really struck a nerve.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:34.260
Yeah, must have. What's the miso soup for?

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:36.100
They did not have soba broth.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.190
What? So you're eating them with miso soup?

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:40.550
How long must this stand?

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.370
Do you have to let soba noodles stand?

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:44.800
No! I mean, the situation with Fujiko.

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:48.100
We still have no idea what 
she is doing in that bathroom.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:51.910
Why do you not force her out, as is 
your right as the tenant of this apartment?

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.140
You think she'll actually listen?

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:56.670
Use your right as the Goemon 
of this apartment to chase her out!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.130
I...

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:06.620
You really don't wanna, do you?

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.710
Hey, Lupin.

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:11.410
Do you have anything long and thin?

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:12.860
Long and thin?

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:13.840
Nope!

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:15.230
Even some chopsticks would do.

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:16.360
We do not have any!

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:19.120
What's his problem?

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:24.230
Fujiko... What exactly do you need 
something long and thin for?

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:26.770
What does it matter?

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.350
Fujiko?

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:33.110
He seriously doesn't remember...

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.390
Coming!

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.990
That's not the repairman.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:43.950
Lupin! The bathroom—

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:45.170
Bonjour!

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:48.770
Sorry to bother you, sir. 
The name's Zenigata.

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:50.310
How can I help you?

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:54.660
Well, I was in the area and smelled
the wonderful aroma of miso soup!

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.820
I found myself attracted to the scent.

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.650
A truly wondrous smell.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:02.710
And I haven't had any 
Japanese food in so long.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:05.960
They don't even sell 
sushi around these parts!

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:07.750
Exactly!

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:13.680
Pardon me! Did you just 
hear my stomach growl?

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:17.160
Well, you just hang on a second there, sonny.

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:18.000
What?

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:19.950
Oh, sir, really, don't mind me!

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:26.120
You'll have to forgive the mess.

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:28.320
Oh, no worries! 
You've been very kind to me...

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:29.170
Whoa, hot!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:33.590
Could he possibly have tracked us down?

00:14:33.590 --> 00:14:35.330
Even if it <i>was</i> just a coincidence,

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.870
Zenigata's got a sharp nose
in more ways than one.

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:38.900
Lupin!

00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:43.390
Ever hear that name before, sir?

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:45.550
Uh, no, can't say I have.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:48.730
Well, when I say Lupin, I mean Lupin III!

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:51.840
You might not have heard 
of him around here...

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:56.580
Oh, Lupin III? Yeah, even out here 
in the sticks, we know the name.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:15:01.240
He's some horrid master crook
who can swipe anything.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.840
Not exactly, sir.

00:15:04.430 --> 00:15:09.500
It's true that he's a criminal and should 
be behind bars, but he's more than that.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:15.350
I wouldn't class him as your 
average law-breaking scumbag.

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:19.070
Pops...

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:25.540
I-I mean, since you "popped" in, 
would you like some soba noodles, too?

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:27.600
Soba noodles! I'd love some!

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:33.830
I can't believe you invited Zenigata in.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:37.540
If I'd chased him off, it would've
 made him even more suspicious.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.830
Make sure he doesn't hang 
about once he's had his fill.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:40.610
Yeah.

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:41.620
Excuse me...

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:45.040
Is it all right if I use your bathroom?

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:45.920
The bathroom?

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:48.820
The toilet's out of action 
at the moment, sadly.

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:52.150
I see. Well, I suppose I'll step out for a sec.

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:54.370
Is there someone else in there?

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:54.940
Well...

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:56.590
I'd love to say hello.

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:57.960
No, best not.

00:15:57.960 --> 00:15:58.940
But, sir...

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:03.000
He's incredibly shy. 
A bit of a shut-in, to be honest.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:06.950
If he saw you, it'd probably be too 
much for his poor heart, Inspector!

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.600
I see...

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:15.010
I never mentioned I was 
a police inspector, did I?

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:24.010
Well, everyone who's heard of Lupin knows 
Inspector Zenigata is hot on his tail!

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:25.700
Oh, that makes sense!

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:28.340
Boy, that's embarrassing!

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:32.290
He'll be back, y'know?

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:33.930
Just don't let him in next time.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:36.230
I can't do that and you know it.

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:38.490
What if he realizes who you are?

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.090
We run.

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:41.720
Yeah, figures.

00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:46.420
Fujiko...

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:50.120
Worried about the thing 
you've got stashed in the toilet?

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:51.660
Dunno what you mean.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.250
Come on, Fujiko.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:58.160
I'm not even saying I want in on the action.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:02.320
If it's important, I'll hang on to it for you. 
If it's dangerous, I'll help you deal with it.

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:06.750
You really can't tell me?

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:08.260
I mean...

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:12.130
I'll be back in a sec.

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:14.130
Where are you going?

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:15.650
The bathroom.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:19.500
The bathroom, okay?! 
I need to use the bathroom!

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:21.680
We can hardly trust you to go in there alone.

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:22.630
And why not?!

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:24.680
I seriously need to use it!

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:26.780
Let me use the bathroom in your room, then!

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:28.640
Would you rather I just went on the floor?!

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:30.980
Well, let's not rule that out...

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:31.660
Idiot!

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:36.660
Fine, I get it already.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:39.820
Hurry it up!

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.860
Is that really the tone you wanna 
take when asking for a favor?

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.660
Please, help me!

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.560
That's not something 
you hear her say too often.

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:53.670
I fear what form her vengeance will take.

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.810
Okay, now's our chance.

00:17:55.810 --> 00:17:57.940
If you could do the honors, Sensei.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:00.180
If poking doesn't work, cutting will!

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:01.670
I refuse.

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:03.430
Why?

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:04.430
It is a worthless endeavor.

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:08.920
Are you telling me you see 
no worth in having a working toilet?!

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.680
I have finally returned!

00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:13.160
That was fast...

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.070
Should I cut him?

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:15.300
We'll cut our way out!

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:16.450
What do you want me to do?

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:18.690
Get in the kitchen and 
get the soba noodles ready!

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:19.570
Understood!

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:21.200
Let's make this good!

00:18:23.650 --> 00:18:24.960
Coming!

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:27.620
Just give me a second...

00:18:58.020 --> 00:18:59.760
I've had all I can take.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:02.560
You can come out now.

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:05.920
Did Zenigata say anything?

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:09.810
I think I did a fine job, but...

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:10.500
Yeah...

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:15.530
"I've had udon noodles in miso before, 
but never soba! It's delicious!"

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:16.740
That's what he said.

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:21.500
What's this?

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.140
Zenigata finally left?

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.650
Hey, nice job earlier.

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:34.380
Where is Fujiko?

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:37.150
She didn't come back here?

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:47.680
Dammit! She's made off with it!

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:55.790
Fujicakes!

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:59.290
Honestly, Lupin! 
You're three sheets to the wind.

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:02.290
You couldn't wait for me to turn up 
before starting the festivities?

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:06.510
Today is our...

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:08.800
Hey, Lupin! Grab some ice!

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:12.290
Pipe down! I'm not your iceman!

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:13.720
Hold it, Lupin.

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:22.950
Oh, come on! You don't remember 
what day it is, do you?

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:27.960
Wh-What was it again?

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:29.720
Unbelievable!

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:49.530
Idiot.

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:18.240
I'm Fujiko Mine.

00:22:18.830 --> 00:22:23.730
Lupin receives a challenge from 
multimillionaire, Zylberstein.

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:28.450
The assassin he's hired is an ex-mercenary who 
specializes in sniping, by the name of Mirage.

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:32.120
Jigen, do you know anything 
about this Mirage guy?

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:35.780
And not even a hello after meeting 
up again? That's awfully cold.

00:22:36.210 --> 00:22:37.530
Isn't it, Jigen?

00:22:37.990 --> 00:22:41.020
Next time: A 7.62 mm Mirage.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:45.000
<b>A 7.62 mm Mirage</b>

00:22:41.020 --> 00:22:44.200
Is this one of those "We don't need 
words; we have guns" kinda deals?
